# Cordova plugins for Capacitor
capacitor-cordova-ios-plugins

# NOTE — three paths Capacitor's template ignores by default are deliberately NOT ignored
# here: App/App/public, App/App/capacitor.config.json and App/App/config.xml.
#
# The template assumes whoever opens the project can run `npx cap sync` to regenerate them.
# This project's whole point is that the Mac has no Node and needs zero terminal steps, so a
# clean clone must already contain the bundled web assets and both configs — without them
# Xcode fails the build with "Command Ld failed" and "capacitor.config.json: no such file".
#
# Consequence: after any web release, re-stage ios-www, run `npx cap sync ios`, and COMMIT
# the regenerated public/ and configs. They are tracked now, so they will not update
# themselves.
